{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And the waters prevailed upon the earth one hundred and fifty days.</b> Scripture spoke according to Noah's perception, as though the waters had not diminished until the ark rested on the mountains of Ararat. But the truth is they began to diminish from the 28th of Sivan, when the rains ceased — as it proceeds to arrange: 'and the rain from heaven was restrained'; immediately <b>and the waters returned from off the earth</b> etc. And the waters diminished at the end of one hundred and fifty days from when the flood began, which is from the 17th of Iyyar until the 17th of Tishrei; then the waters had diminished enough for the ark to rest. Immediately <b>and the ark rested in the month</b> — Tishrei, on the 17th day of the month etc. <b>On the tenth</b> — this is Tevet, on the first of the month the tops of the mountains were seen. 'And it came to pass at the end of forty days' that the tops of the mountains were seen — this is the 11th of Shevat — 'and Noah opened the window of the ark which he had made'; and he sent the raven after seven days, as Rashi explained, which is the 18th of Shevat; and he sent the dove. <b>And he waited yet another seven days, and again sent the dove</b> — this is the 25th of Shevat. <b>And he waited yet another seven days</b> — this is the 2nd of Adar — and he sent the dove, and it did not return to him again. And he stayed in the ark 28 days until the 1st of Nisan, as it says: 'And it came to pass in the one and six hundredth year, in Nisan, on the first of the month, the waters dried up,' and he removed the covering of the ark and looked, and behold <b>the waters were dried up</b> from off the face of the ground. But there was still mud and mire, and it was not fit for the tread of a foot until the 27th of Iyyar, as it is written: 'and in the second month, on the 27th day of the month, the earth was dry.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:27.676826304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}